From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 127] panvk: decode BC7 once per block for the ASTC transcode
Generated-by: LLM

The BC7 transcoder re-ran the full per-mode BC7 decode for every texel
of every pass (16x per pass), spilling ~9000 values per thread. Parse
mode, partition, rotation, endpoints and p-bits once per block and fetch
each texel with a few bit operations; feed the same streaming candidate
search as patch 126. The decoder matches the previous one bit-exactly on
all eight modes. The search's mean and covariance now come from one pass
(E[pp^T] - mean mean^T) instead of two, for BC1-BC5 too. biblioklept

Mali-G615 MC2, one 2048x2048 level: BC7 1066 -> 174 ms (random blocks),
514 -> 142 ms (realistic blocks), BC3 80 -> 69 ms, BC5 113 -> 104 ms
(synthetic worst cases), PSNR unchanged.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/126

